    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/College-of-Medicine/Senior-Advisor-for-Research-Administration-and-Transition_REQ_0000083050-3": {
      "title": "Senior Advisor for Research Administration and Transition",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants .   JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS Senior Advisor for Research Administration and Transition   The College of Medicine invites applications for a part-time academic (non-exempt) job of Associate Professor, Senior Advisor for Research Administration and Transition. The Senior Advisor for Research Administration provides strategic counsel, institutional knowledge, and transition support to ensure a seamless transfer of leadership and continuity of research administration operations during the onboarding of the new Associate Dean for Research Administration. Job duties to include: Provide onboarding and mentoring support to the incoming Associate Dean for Research Administration. Facilitate the transfer of institutional knowledge, historical context, and best practices related to research administration, compliance, and faculty support. Ensure continuity and uninterrupted support of research faculty, trainees, and students in matters related to research administration during the leadership transition. Advise on stakeholder relationships and key internal and external partnerships. Provide guidance on complex research administration matters, including faculty development, proposal support, compliance, and research operations. Assist with the evaluation and prioritization of ongoing initiatives during the transition period. Undertake special assignments related to research strategy, administrative effectiveness, and organizational development. Serve as the Institutional Official for the IACUC. Preferred Requirements, qualifications, education and/or competencies: Prior experience serving as an Associate Dean for Research Administration or an equivalent senior research leadership position. Comprehensive knowledge of the College of Medicine, Penn State University, and Penn State Health research enterprise, strategic priorities, and organizational cultures. Thorough knowledge of institutional research policies, procedures, governance structures, and external funding environments. Excellent interpersonal, communication, and relationship-building skills.   BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
    },
    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/College-of-Medicine/Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor---Cell-and-Biological-Systems_REQ_0000082467-2": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Cell and Biological Systems",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants .   POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Cell and Biological Systems at the Penn State University College of Medicine invites applications from outstanding Ph.D. and/or M.D. scientists for a tenure-track position, to be filled at the rank of Assistant or Associate or Full Professor.  The Department is within the thriving research environment of the College of Medicine and the renowned Milton S. Hershey Medical Center, located in Hershey, Pennsylvania. The Department has broad strengths in cellular and molecular approaches toward basic and translational research. The search welcomes applicants with strong records of research accomplishment in any areas of biomedical research that may complement and/or expand the research interests of the Department. The Department has a range of research focus areas including inflammation and innate immunity; virology; cellular signaling and metabolism; structure/function of membrane proteins; cytoskeleton and contractile proteins; mitochondria function and dynamics; microvascular regulation; diabetes; neurodegeneration; and cancer biology. The Department enjoys strong interactions with the Penn State Cancer Institute, the Heart and Vascular Institute, the Institute for Personalized Medicine, the NIH-supported Clinical and Translational Science Institute, and the outstanding Core Facilities and Research Resources within the Penn State College of Medicine.  The on-campus Cryo-EM Center houses state-of-the-art equipment, such as a Titan Krios microscope and a Hydra Bio Plasma-Focus Ion Beam scanning electron microscope. The faculty candidate will be an outstanding scientist holding a Ph.D. and/or M.D. The applicant will have a strong record of research accomplishment in any areas of biomedical research that may complement and/or expand the research interests of the Department.   The candidate will have an independent research program and a record of accomplishments such as outstanding publications and a record of external funding. FIELD OF STUDY FOR PHD AND/OR MD: biomedical research DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: The faculty scholar will be required to: -direct a nationally recognized research program in an area biomedical science that complements existing strengths in the Department -attract robust external funding to support the scholar’s research -provide an outstanding environment for training students and postdoctoral fellows -teach in the graduate and medical curriculum -participate in administrative service to the Department, College, and University To enhance the scholar’s national/international reputation, the faculty member will be encouraged to: -present their work at research conferences or seminars -publish manuscripts -participate in peer review for journals and grant panels -serve in leadership roles in scientific societies The position provides a competitive start-up package, excellent laboratory space, and a strong and supportive research environment. Additionally, excellent benefits and a safe, friendly and inclusive work environment make the Penn State College of Medicine and the Hershey area an outstanding location to live and work. The Hershey Medical Center is a strong community of health professionals, situated in Hershey, PA, with great schools, excellent housing and close proximity to Philadelphia, Baltimore and Washington DC. Further information about the Department, research interests of faculty, and the successful and appealing Hershey research environment is provided at the Department website: https://med.psu.edu/departments-faculty/cell-and-biological-systems .   BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES This position requires the following clearances in addition to applicable background checks: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check. Due to the financial and fiduciary responsibilities of this position, successful completion of a credit history check will be required in addition to standard background checks.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
    },
    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/College-of-Medicine/Assistant-Professor---Surgery_REQ_0000081799-2": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Surgery",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants .   POSITION SPECIFICS Title:                Assistant/Associate Professor Department:    Surgery / Plastic Surgery FLSA:              Faculty- Tenure Track eligible Summary of Job: The Department of Surgery at Penn State College of Medicine in Hershey, PA, seeks an innovative tissue engineer or regenerative medicine scientist at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor (tenure track-eligible) to establish an internationally recognized program in regenerative surgery with emphasis on cardiovascular tissue engineering. The successful candidate shall have a track record of funding from the National Institutes of Health and have a strong publication record. They shall have experience as a principal investigator managing a multi-disciplinary team. It is expected that the selected candidate will develop collaborative research programs spanning regenerative medicine, biomaterials, stem cell biology, biofabrication, and translational large-animal models. A major expectation of the position is close collaboration with the Department's cardiovascular surgery, transplantation, and biomedical engineering programs to develop biologically integrated therapies that promote myocardial recovery in patients supported with next-generation mechanical circulatory support devices, including wireless ventricular assist devices. The successful candidate will join an interdisciplinary team of surgeons, physician-scientists, and engineers committed to translating innovative technologies from bench to bedside. Candidates holding a PhD or comparable scientific degree with specialty and expertise in one or more of the following are encouraged to apply: Cardiac tissue engineering Biomaterials Stem cell biology Extracellular matrix biology Mechanobiology Biofabrication and 3D bioprinting Drug or biologic delivery systems Regenerative medicine, wound healing, and reconstructive surgery Translational cardiovascular research The successful candidate will: Establish an independently funded tissue engineering laboratory. Develop NIH-funded translational research programs. Collaborate with cardiac surgeons, plastic surgeons, transplant surgeons, and biomedical engineers. Develop regenerative strategies to promote myocardial recovery during mechanical circulatory support. Participate in large-animal translational studies. Mentor graduate students, postdoctoral scholars, medical students, residents, and junior faculty. Develop multidisciplinary collaborations across Penn State College of Medicine and University Park. Publish in high-impact scientific journals. Participate in technology development and commercialization. The Department is willing to offer a start-up package for the appropriate candidate and is committed to their success.  Candidates must provide proof of education or having ABD status for a PhD in the requested discipline by the time of hire. Interested candidates should apply on-line and provide a detailed CV with 2-3 references.   BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
